    "metadata": {
      "name": "EventGraph",
      "description": "A boss that extends AdvEnemyBase.",
      "version": "1.0.0",
      "created_at": "2026-11-14T00:00:00Z",
      "modified_at": "2026-11-14T00:00:00Z"
    },
    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "ADVANCED 5/9: CLASS INHERITANCE (the boss)\nBlueprint classes do not share graphs, so \"inheritance\" is a CONTRACT: this class declares\n`AdvEnemyBase` as its parent (Class Settings > Parent, stored as blueprint_metadata.parent_class) and\nkeeps the parent's events (`take_damage`, `died`) with identical names and parameters. Anything\nthat talks to an AdvEnemyBase through those events also works on the boss. The boss then EXTENDS\nthe behaviour: armor, a second phase, minions. Compare with AdvEnemyBase.class side by side.\nComposition (an enemy HAS a mesh, a collider, a health bar) is done with components in the class\nprefab; shared logic that should not be copied lives in macros (see AdvMacroLibrary).",
        "position": [
          0,
          -330
        ],
        "size": [
          1500,
          230
        ],
        "color": [
          0.9,
          0.75,
          0.2,
          0.28
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "1. BEGIN PLAY - announce the spawn.",
        "position": [
          -40,
          -80
        ],
        "size": [
          680,
          270
        ],
        "color": [
          0.25,
          0.45,
          0.75,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "bp",
          "bp_log"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-3",
        "text": "2. THE CONTRACT: take_damage(amount) - damage reduced by armor with a floor of 1\n(Max(amount - armor, 1) so a high armor never makes the enemy immortal), subtracted from health,\nand `died` is dispatched at zero or below.\nBOSS EXTENSION: when still alive and below 250 health, a Do Once guard enters phase 2\nexactly one time (Do Once remembers it already fired; without it every later hit would\nrestart the phase).",
        "position": [
          -30,
          390
        ],
        "size": [
          3380,
          940
        ],
        "color": [
          0.25,
          0.65,
          0.35,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "td",
          "td_armor",
          "td_sub",
          "td_max",
          "td_hp",
          "td_hp_sub",
          "td_set",
          "td_dead",
          "td_if",
          "td_died",
          "td_once",
          "td_low",
          "td_phase_if",
          "td_phase"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-4",
        "text": "3. DEATH - log and remove this object from the world (its own entity comes from this class's\nTransform). Subclasses may replace this: a boss would also drop loot.",
        "position": [
          -40,
          1760
        ],
        "size": [
          1020,
          500
        ],
        "color": [
          0.8,
          0.3,
          0.3,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "dd",
          "dd_log",
          "dd_self",
          "dd_kill"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-5",
        "text": "4. BOSS ONLY: enter_phase(phase) - a new event the base does not have. Store the phase, harden\nthe armor by 5 and run a For Loop three times to spawn three minion objects. A For Loop's `Body`\nwire runs once per iteration; it has no Completed pin, so put \"after the loop\" work BEFORE it\nor in a Sequence.",
        "position": [
          -30,
          2460
        ],
        "size": [
          2360,
          480
        ],
        "color": [
          0.6,
          0.35,
          0.75,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "ph",
          "ph_set",
          "ph_armor",
          "ph_up",
          "ph_set_armor",
          "ph_log",
          "ph_loop",
          "ph_minion"
        ]
      }
    ],
